    "text": "A person lives in a high-rise building on the bank of a river $50 \\mathrm{~m}$ wide. Across the river is a well lit tower of height $40 \\mathrm{~m}$. When the person, who is at a height of $10 \\mathrm{~m}$, looks through a polarizer at an appropriate angle at light of the tower reflecting from the river surface, he notes that intensity of light coming from distance $\\mathrm{X}$ from his building is the least and this corresponds to the light coming from light bulbs at height ' $\\mathrm{Y}$ ' on the tower. The values of $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ are respectively close to (refractive index of water $\\simeq \\frac{4}{3}$ )\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/w_KVq_jn1q4obXVY-2dEduDQaUddFg3sAsKTqxmLnsM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
